# CREDENTIALS.manifest — the single source of truth for intake operator credentials.
#
# `engine intake doctor`, `engine intake setup`, and the generated `.env.example`
# all DERIVE from this file — so the thing built to fight onboarding drift does not
# itself drift. Edit here; never hand-edit `.env.example` (regenerate it).
#
# Format: one record per line, fields pipe-delimited, blank lines and #-comments skipped.
#   key       env var name (or a synthetic BIN_*/mcp-name for non-env rows)
#   service   human label for grouping
#   required  req | triage | boards | optional
#               req    → a missing one FAILS the doctor (non-zero exit; gates callers)
#               triage → needed only when a wave hits the read-only DB (WARN)
#               boards → needed only to publish Decision/Outcomes boards (WARN)
#               optional → nice-to-have (WARN)
#   secret    true → never seeded, never written to a committed file
#   default   non-secret default value (seeded into `dotfile` if absent), or empty
#   dotfile   PREFERRED gitignored home — where a FRESH value is written (doctor seed /
#               setup wizard); secrets are only ever written to `.env.local`. NOT the only
#               place it is read: every file-key row resolves .env.local → .env (project
#               dotfiles only), so `.env.local` can hold everything and an existing
#               `.env` still works.
#               A row stays on `.env` only when an out-of-band reader is pinned to it
#               (PROVE_S3_* — skills/prove/assets/_prove-s3-env.sh reads the nearest .env).
#   how       one-line how-to-get / fix hint (printed on a miss)
#   check     how the doctor verifies presence:
#               file-key       env var set OR a searched dotfile contains KEY= (seedable if non-secret + default)
#               env-present    env var set only (no dotfile; e.g. an SSO/shell-exported value)
#               binary:<name>  `command -v <name>` succeeds
#               mcp:<name>     `claude mcp list` shows <name> Connected
#               note           informational only — never pass/fail, never affects exit code
#
# key|service|required|secret|default|dotfile|how|check
SLACK_INTAKE_TOKEN|Slack|req|true||.env.local|Create a Slack app + bot token with scopes chat:write, channels:read, groups:read; paste the xoxb- token into .env.local (fallback env: SLACK_BOT_TOKEN)|file-key
SLACK_INTAKE_CHANNEL|Slack|optional|false||.env.local|Fallback announce channel NAME (e.g. #intake). Per-project channels come from INBOX_REGISTRY; this is only a default|file-key
SLACK_INTAKE_CONTEXT_LOOKBACK_DAYS|Slack|optional|false|7|.env.local|Lookback window (days) for the Phase-1 channel-context read (engine slack-read --history). Per-project override; the channel LIST lives in the project Inbox Handbook|file-key
linear-server|Linear (MCP)|req|false|||Interactive OAuth in Claude Code: add the Linear HTTP MCP (mcp.linear.app/mcp) and complete browser consent. All /intake WRITES (save_comment, save_status_update, documents) are MCP-only|mcp:linear-server
LINEAR_API_KEY|Linear (GraphQL read)|optional|true||.env.local|Linear personal API key (lin_api_...) from Linear Settings > API. Enables engine project fetch / ticket-search read path; the MCP covers reads otherwise (fail-soft)|file-key
AWS_PROFILE|AWS / SSM|triage|false|||Run `aws sso login --profile <name>` for the staging profile, then export AWS_PROFILE. Gates the read-only DB tunnel (scripts/staging-db-tunnel.sh) used by triage|env-present
AWS_REGION|AWS / SSM|triage|false|us-east-2|.env|AWS region for the staging profile (default us-east-2)|file-key
BIN_AWS|AWS CLI v2|triage|false|||Install AWS CLI v2 — the `aws` binary is required by scripts/staging-db-tunnel.sh|binary:aws
BIN_SESSION_MANAGER_PLUGIN|AWS SSM plugin|triage|false|||Install session-manager-plugin (Session Manager plugin) — required alongside aws for the SSM port-forward tunnel|binary:session-manager-plugin
FINCH_DB_RO_SECRET|Read-only DB|triage|false|staging/finch/db-ro-url||Secrets Manager secret NAME holding the read-only data_ro postgres URL. Fetched at runtime (aws secretsmanager get-secret-value), host re-pointed to 127.0.0.1:15432. NEVER stored in a dotfile. Runbook: docs/runbooks/staging-db-ro-analyst.md|note
PROVE_S3_BUCKET|S3 board publish|boards|false|staging-finch-proofs|.env|S3 bucket for published Decision/Outcomes boards|file-key
PROVE_S3_REGION|S3 board publish|boards|false|us-east-2|.env|S3 region for board publish|file-key
PROVE_S3_PREFIX|S3 board publish|boards|false|proofs|.env|S3 key prefix for board publish|file-key
PROVE_S3_PROFILE|S3 board publish|boards|false|finch-staging|.env|AWS profile used to presign board writes (reuses the staging SSO creds)|file-key
TEMPORAL_HOST|Temporal (tangential)|optional|false||.env|Temporal host (temporal.<env>.finch.local) for the optional visibility tunnel; not on the core intake path|file-key
TEMPORAL_PORT|Temporal (tangential)|optional|false|7233|.env|Temporal port (default 7233) for the optional visibility tunnel|file-key
notion|Notion (MCP)|optional|false|||Interactive OAuth for the Notion HTTP MCP (mcp.notion.com/mcp). Only needed at project creation / KB maintenance. No CLI fallback|mcp:notion
POSTHOG|PostHog|optional|false|||UNWIRED: no env var or CLI exists today. PostHog-sourced signals are handled manually via the PostHog UI. Listed so onboarding knows it is deliberately not automated|note
